      synthetic.honest_helpers = 2; dry-run-fork.txt shows the spec). Nothing may outlive its job: any unproven end FAILs P5.
  Order: the safe host scope check (below) first, then (A) if not yet run on this host, then (B). One at a time.
  RUN ON A HOST THAT IS NOT CPU-STARVED (the end-of-job proof's latency grows with starvation: gate 15 measured proofs up to
  ~126 s on a starved test host; rehearsals here: p99 2.2 s).
  DEFAULT LIMITS (nothing in the shipped spec changes them): an end not proven within verify_timeout = 120 s is reported
  Unverified and stays in quarantine (re-hunted; `unverified_end_cleared` when proven later: not a FAIL by itself);
  after resources.unproven_end_limit_s = 600 s the attempt gets the note `unproven_end` (processes named, lease released,
  the run ends exit 8): that note FAILs P5.

THE END-OF-JOB PROOF (round 10 gate13c G13c-M1; round 11 gate14 G14-M1; wording round 12 gate15 m15-manifest; RUNBOOK
2.10): the hunt follows the supervisor's own children, every member it stopped, and every WALKED process: a live process
OF OUR UID, started after the job, outside every job session and without the job's marker (never signalled). It never
follows the descendants of a process it does not walk (a process classified as not the job's: another uid, another
attempt's or campaign's marker, the supervisor's own session, older than the job). At every level it follows, a listed
process that ended between the listing and its examination, and may have handed off to a successor born after the
listing, is never counted as absent: the fixed point looks again, and a proof pass that sees one (or a walked process that
ended, or a walked list that changed) is inconclusive. Exempt only by a conclusive fact: a member the hunt stopped and
killed (pid AND start time); a zombie already seen ended in an earlier listing of the same hunt; a process started before
the job; a zombie of the supervisor's own session; a process classified as not the job's AND not walked; a zombie of
another job's session whose leader is held unreaped AND was born no later than it. A gone entry (no start time) is always
a suspect. A scope still populated with no live member listed gets cgroup.kill. A proof that stays inconclusive ends as an
unverified / unproven end (P5), never as a proven one. What a proof says: no marked process of the job and no member of
its session is alive in the supervisor's tree, below any number of WALKED marker-less processes of our uid, at two
conclusive passes; it says nothing about descendants of a process the hunt does not walk, nor about a marker-less process
that re-sets the marker for new children (out of scope since procfix3).

